{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>The scepter shall not depart from Judah.</b> Midrash Aggadah: לא יסור — לא יפרח, like סורי הגפן (the shoots of the vine), נכריה — which is like the branches of the vine." "<b>Until Shiloh come.</b> Until the Tabernacle of Shiloh is destroyed — יבא in the sense of destruction, like לא יבא עוד. This is its meaning: no king shall sprout or flourish in Judah until the Tabernacle of Shiloh is abandoned, and so it says: ״ויטש משכן שילה״, and next to it: ״ויבחר בדוד עבדו״. Another interpretation: The kingdom shall not depart from the house of David to give it to another, as it departed from Saul — ״עד כי יבא שילה״, the King Messiah — and all the more so when Messiah comes, since Messiah son of David he is; thus it turns out it shall never depart. As it is said: ״ונאמן ביתך וממלכה עד עולם״, and it is written: ״וחסדי לא אסיר מעמו כאשר הסירותי מעם שאול״. Another interpretation: לא יסור שבט מיהודה — he shall not rule over all Israel — עד כי יבא שילה, meaning at Shechem, for there the kingdom was divided, and Shiloh and Shechem were close to each other, as it is written: ״בין שילה ובין שכם״. Therefore it uses 'Shiloh.' But in any event, ״ולו יקהת עמים״ — after the kingdom was divided. Another interpretation: לא יסור שבט מיהודה ומחוקק מבין רגליו — עד, meaning forever, עד כי יבא שילה — for behold Messiah will come, and he is of his tribe. From the Rabbi, Rabbi Yitzhak."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:28.412551771Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}